  </td>
  <td>
  <div id=3DPPTP2 class=3DPTxt><font size=3D2><a
  href=3D"javascript:GoToSld('slide0125.htm');" id=3DPPTL2>Point Operations=
 on
  Histograms</a></font></div>
  <div id=3DPPTC2 class=3DCTxt style=3D'display:none'><font size=3D2>
  <ul>
   <li>Suppose we have a monotonic level operation such that</li>
   <li>f(a) =3D a<font face=3DSymbol>&cent;</font></li>
   <li><font face=3DTimes>f(b) =3D b</font><font face=3DSymbol>&cent;</font=
></li>
   <li><font face=3DTimes>Then the histogram H become H</font><font face=3D=
Symbol>&cent;</font><font
       face=3DTimes> such that:</font></li>
   <li>H(g)dg =3D<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;&nbsp; </span>H(g)d=
g</li>
  </ul>
  </font></div>
  </td>
 </tr>
 <tr onmouseover=3D"Over(this)" onmouseout=3D"Out(this)" onclick=3D"Follow(=
this)"
  style=3D'cursor:hand'>
  <td align=3Dright valign=3Dtop>
  <div class=3DsldNum><font size=3D2>3</font></div>
  </td>
  <td>
  <div id=3DPPTP3 class=3DPTxt><font size=3D2><a
  href=3D"javascript:GoToSld('slide0126.htm');" id=3DPPTL3>Point Operations=
 on
  Histograms (cont.)</a></font></div>
  <div id=3DPPTC3 class=3DCTxt style=3D'display:none'><font size=3D2>
  <ul>
   <li>Let b =3D a + D for some very small D.</li>
   <li>Then<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>f (b) <font
       face=3DSymbol>&raquo;</font><font face=3DTimes> f(a) + f</font><font
       face=3DSymbol>&cent;</font><font face=3DTimes> (a)D.</font></li>
   <li>Thus</li>
   <li>		H(g)dg =3D<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </sp=
an>H(g)dg</li>
   <li>or approximating:</li>
   <li>		H(a)D<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span><font face=3DS=
ymbol>&raquo;</font><font
       face=3DTimes> <span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;</span>H</font>=
<font
       face=3DSymbol>&cent;</font><font face=3DTimes> (a</font><font face=
=3DSymbol>&cent;</font><font
       face=3DTimes> ) f</font><font face=3DSymbol>&cent;</font><font face=
=3DTimes> (a)D</font></li>
   <li>		H<font face=3DSymbol>&cent;</font><font face=3DTimes> (a</font><fo=
nt
       face=3DSymbol>&cent;</font><font face=3DTimes> ) </font><font face=
=3DSymbol>&raquo;</font><font
       face=3DTimes><span
       style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp=
;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
       </span>=3D</font></li>
   <li>		H<font face=3DSymbol>&cent;</font><font face=3DTimes> (g)<span
       style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>=3D</font></li>
  </ul>
  </font></div>
  </td>
 </tr>
 <tr onmouseover=3D"Over(this)" onmouseout=3D"Out(this)" onclick=3D"Follow(=
this)"
  style=3D'cursor:hand'>
  <td align=3Dright valign=3Dtop>
  <div class=3DsldNum><font size=3D2>4</font></div>
  </td>
  <td>
  <div id=3DPPTP4 class=3DPTxt><font size=3D2><a
  href=3D"javascript:GoToSld('slide0128.htm');" id=3DPPTL4>Histogram Equali=
zation</a></font></div>
  <div id=3DPPTC4 class=3DCTxt style=3D'display:none'><font size=3D2>
  <ul>
   <li>Automatic contrast enhancment:</li>
   <li>Basic Idea: allocate the most ouput levels to the most frequently
       occuring inputs.</li>
   <li>Look at the histogram of the input signal.</li>
   <li>If we allocate output levels proportional to the frequency of occurr=
ence
       for our input levels, the output histogram should be uniform.</li>
   <li>This process is know as histogram equalization</li>
  </ul>
  </font></div>
  </td>
 </tr>
 <tr onmouseover=3D"Over(this)" onmouseout=3D"Out(this)" onclick=3D"Follow(=
this)"
  style=3D'cursor:hand'>
  <td align=3Dright valign=3Dtop>
  <div class=3DsldNum><font size=3D2>5</font></div>
  </td>
  <td>
  <div id=3DPPTP5 class=3DPTxt><font size=3D2><a
  href=3D"javascript:GoToSld('slide0129.htm');" id=3DPPTL5>Histogram Equali=
zation</a></font></div>
  <div id=3DPPTC5 class=3DCTxt style=3D'display:none'><font size=3D2>
  <ul>
   <li>We want a flat (constant) output histogram:</li>
   <li>	H<font face=3DSymbol>&cent;</font><font face=3DTimes> (g) =3D<span
       style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp=
;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
       </span>=3D A<sub>0</sub> / g<sub>max</sub></font></li>
   <li>Thus:</li>
   <li>	 f<font face=3DSymbol>&cent;</font><font face=3DTimes> (g) =3D<span
       style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
       </span>H(g)<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span></font><fo=
nt
       face=3DWingdings>&agrave;</font><font face=3DTimes><span
       style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span>f(g) =3D<span
       style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp=
;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
       </span>H(x)dx</font></li>
   <li>where</li>
   <ul>
    <ul>
     <li>g is the input (graylevl).</li>
     <li>g<sub>max</sub> is the maximum input.</li>
     <li>A<sub>0</sub> is the image area (area of objects with graylevel <f=
ont
         face=3DSymbol>&sup3;</font><font face=3DTimes> 0)</font></li>
     <li>f(g) is the output graylevel.</li>
    </ul>
   </ul>
  </ul>
  </font></div>
  </td>
 </tr>
 <tr onmouseover=3D"Over(this)" onmouseout=3D"Out(this)" onclick=3D"Follow(=
this)"
  style=3D'cursor:hand'>
  <td align=3Dright valign=3Dtop>
  <div class=3DsldNum><font size=3D2>6</font></div>
  </td>
  <td>
  <div id=3DPPTP6 class=3DPTxt><font size=3D2><a
  href=3D"javascript:GoToSld('slide0156.htm');" id=3DPPTL6>Histogram Equali=
zation</a></font></div>
  <div id=3DPPTC6 class=3DCTxt style=3D'display:none'><font size=3D2>
  <ul>
   <li>However, the probability density function is the normalized histogra=
m (i.e.,
       p(g) =3D H(g) / A<sub>0</sub>):</li>
   <br>
   <br>
   <ul>
    <li>f(g) =3D g<sub>max</sub><span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;&nbs=
p;
        </span>p(x)dx <span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;</span>=3D g<s=
ub>max</sub>
        P(g)</li>
    <br>
    <br>
   </ul>
   <li>where</li>
   <ul>
    <ul>
     <li>p is the probability density function (normalized histogram) of the
         input image.</li>
     <li>P is the cumulative probability density function.</li>
     <br>
     <br>
    </ul>
   </ul>
  </ul>
  </font></div>
  </td>
 </tr>
 <tr onmouseover=3D"Over(this)" onmouseout=3D"Out(this)" onclick=3D"Follow(=
this)"
  style=3D'cursor:hand'>
  <td align=3Dright valign=3Dtop>
  <div class=3DsldNum><font size=3D2>7</font></div>
  </td>
  <td>
  <div id=3DPPTP7 class=3DPTxt><font size=3D2><a
  href=3D"javascript:GoToSld('slide0149.htm');" id=3DPPTL7>Adaptive Histogr=
am
  Equalization</a></font></div>
  <div id=3DPPTC7 class=3DCTxt style=3D'display:none'><font size=3D2>
  <ul>
   <li>Remap based on local, not global, histogram.</li>
   <li>Allows localized contrast enhancement.</li>
   <li>Example: 13 <font face=3DSymbol>&acute;</font><font face=3DTimes> 13=
 window
       around each pixel.</font></li>
   <li>Problem: ringing artifacts, noise is enhanced.</li>
   <li>(Partial) Solution: constrain the remapping.</li>
  </ul>
  </font></div>
  </td>
 </tr>
 <tr onmouseover=3D"Over(this)" onmouseout=3D"Out(this)" onclick=3D"Follow(=
this)"
  style=3D'cursor:hand'>
  <td align=3Dright valign=3Dtop>
  <div class=3DsldNum><font size=3D2>8</font></div>
  </td>
  <td>
  <div id=3DPPTP8 class=3DPTxt><font size=3D2><a
  href=3D"javascript:GoToSld('slide0150.htm');" id=3DPPTL8>Histogram Matchi=
ng</a></font></div>
  <div id=3DPPTC8 class=3DCTxt style=3D'display:none'><font size=3D2>
  <ul>
   <li>Histogram equalization produces a uniform output histogram.</li>
   <li>We can instead make it whatever we want.</li>
   <li>Use histogram equalization as an intermediate step.</li>
   <ul>
    <li>First equalize the histogram of the input signal:</li>
    <li>f<sub>1</sub>(g) =3D g<sub>max</sub> P<sub>1</sub>(g)</li>
    <li>Then, equalize the desired output histogram:</li>
    <li>f<sub>2</sub>(g) =3D g<sub>max</sub> P<sub>2</sub>(g)</li>
    <li>Histogram specification (matching) is</li>
    <li>f<sub> </sub>(g) =3D f<sub>2<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp;=
 </span></sub>(f<sub>1</sub>(g))
        =3D P<sub>2<span style=3D'mso-spacerun:yes'>&nbsp; </span></sub>(P<=
sub>1</sub>(g))</li>
   </ul>
   <br>
  </ul>
  </font></div>
  </td>
 </tr>
